---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import SiteHeader from "@/components/SiteHeader.astro";
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy — Loopdeck">
  <div class="flex min-h-screen flex-col">
    <SiteHeader />
    <article class="mx-auto w-full max-w-2xl flex-1 px-4 py-12 leading-relaxed">
      <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground">Last updated: 14 September 2026</p>

      <h2 class="font-serif mt-10 text-2xl font-semibold">What we collect</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-muted-foreground">
        Loopdeck collects your email address when you create an account. Task titles you enter are stored so the product
        can show your backlog and today&apos;s focus.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-serif mt-8 text-2xl font-semibold">Why we collect it</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-muted-foreground">
        Email is used for sign-in and account recovery through our authentication provider. Task data is used only to
        provide the todo service to you.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-serif mt-8 text-2xl font-semibold">Retention</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-muted-foreground">
        Data is kept until you delete your account. When you delete your account, your tasks and profile are removed
        from our database.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-serif mt-8 text-2xl font-semibold">Your rights</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-muted-foreground">
        You can delete your account at any time from the dashboard. This removes your email, tasks, and related records.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-serif mt-8 text-2xl font-semibold">Contact</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-muted-foreground">For privacy questions, contact the project maintainer.</p>

      <p class="mt-10">
        <a href="/auth/signup" class="font-medium text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">
          Back to sign up
        </a>
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>
